pts used: 1/8. Demo requests used: 7/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    counts = {}\n    for row in grid:\n        for x in row:\n            counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1\n    bg = max(counts, key=counts.get)\n    mark = min((x for x in counts if x != bg), key=lambda x: counts[x])\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Marked pixels are a pattern; locate repetitions of that pattern in\n    # background cells, allowing rotations/reflections.\n    pts = [(r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == mark]\n    if not pts:\n        return out\n    transforms = []\n    for flip in (1, -1):\n        for k in range(4):\n            q = []\n            for r, c in pts:\n                x, y = r, flip * c\n                for _ in range(k):\n                    x, y = y, -x\n                q.append((x, y))\n            mr, mc = min(x for x, y in q), min(y for x, y in q)\n            transforms.append(sorted((x-mr, y-mc) for x, y in q))\n\n    shapes = set()\n    for shape in transforms:\n        shapes.add(tuple(shape))\n    for shape in shapes:\n        sh = max(r for r, c in shape) + 1\n        sw = max(c for r, c in shape) + 1\n        for r0 in range(h-sh+1):\n            for c0 in range(w-sw+1):\n                cells = [(r0+r, c0+c) for r, c in shape]\n                if all(grid[r][c] == 0 for r, c in cells):\n                    for r, c in cells:\n                        out[r][c] = mark\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":34,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1790704047.14,"t1":1790704054.99,"alias":"task-6670eb87","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 2.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-6670eb87\nTest input (27x24):\n0 0 6 0 0 6 0 0 6 6 0 6 0 6 6 6 0 0 6 6 0 0 6 0\n6 6 6 0 6 0 6 6 6 0 0 6 0 6 6 0 6 6 6 6 6 6 0 6\n0